 "notes": "Table XV Part II (Bi-lingualism), first page; continues on leaf 259. Records with subsidiary=null are the columns 'Number of persons speaking mother tongue' (cols 2-3, 10-11). Only Males and Females are printed; persons is null. No division/British Territory subtotals are printed; 'Total' row = all areas. Checks: Assamese-speaking Naga Hills Males printed clearly 407 here but 497 in Part I (leaf 249) and the printed Total 1,039,207 (= Part I) requires 497: misprint, kept as printed. Assamese MT / Bengali subsidiary Males: printed Total 15,084 but the legible district figures sum to 14,938 excluding Sadiya ('5?'), implying Sadiya 146 - does not reconcile with the printed '5?' ; kept as printed. Khasi States Females read 52 (last digit faint; 52 makes the column add to 5,015). Assamese MT / Tibeto-Burmese Females: districts add to 599, printed Total 590 (italic, read clearly); kept as printed. Kamrup Males first digit smudged, reads 267 (column then adds to printed 982). Bengali MT / Assamese subsidiary Females: districts add to 13,496, printed Total 13,495 (Sadiya read 50, last digit thin); kept as printed. Bengali-speaking Manipur State Females printed with a damaged first digit ('044'), read 944 as in Part I."
